00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.960
Underneath our Cloud
CDW is Google BigQuery.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:08.520
And Google BigQuery is an
incredibly powerful managed

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.800
database for analytics.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.510
It's a columnar database.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.280
So it works very,
very fast, very,

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.310
very efficiently at analyzing
great big chunks of data

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:23.190
and analyzing time
series types of data

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:27.480
that we often see within
the health care space.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.610
It's fully managed,
which means that you

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.430
don't need to worry about
the infrastructure for it.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:36.330
You just go straight to
cloud.google.com/bigquery,

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:39.390
and it's there ready
for you to use.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.810
And it's safer because
we automatically

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.900
encrypt all of the data
that's in BigQuery.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.930
And the way that we set
up projects on BigQuery

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:54.240
as part of Cloud CDW enables you
to meet your HIPAA compliance

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.680
needs as well.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.260
So we have Deployment
Manager templates

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:02.250
that are set up BigQuery
projects and Google Cloud

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:06.450
projects in a way that helps
you to satisfy your HIPAA

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.509
requirements.

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:13.530
In addition, because
we have these public

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.900
and commercial data
sets available,

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.170
you can integrate these into
the analysis you're doing.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.960
And I'll show you some examples
of those different data sets

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.310
as well.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.650
But most powerfully,
it's scalable.

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.940
So you can throw
petabytes of data at this,

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.020
and it doesn't blink.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.800
Behind the scenes, it
scales up horizontally.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.070
So it's looking ahead at the
analysis you're trying to do,

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.140
and just brings
additional machines,

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.100
additional compute power to bear
as it sees that you need it.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.330
And interestingly, for
a columnar database,

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.180
everything is
queryable through SQL,

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.660
which means that we have
a host of different tools

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.210
that you can use
on top of BigQuery

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.580
directly for doing your
business intelligence

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.830
and your visualization.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.770
Google has its own,
Google Data Studio.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.230
But in addition, all
